{
  "library": "Evani procedural effects",
  "version": 1,
  "about": "The procedural section of the material library: effects the engine draws from code (no textures, no download beyond the module). Each item names the evani.toml module line a game adds to get it, its headline params (the 3-5 sliders the studio shows first), its other params (the Advanced fold) and its presets. A preset is a named set of param values over the item's `base`; applying one puts every param of the item back to its default, then `base`, then the preset (so presets round-trip). Every name is a registered live param (docs/LIVE_API.md): the studio, the Look Lab and AI agents drive the same values with param_set. `stage` is only how the studio's view stages the item (sea bed depth and colour, the water's shape); it is not part of the effect and a game ignores it. Items with status `coming` are planned and not built yet (research 2026-11-01). An item may name its procedural library category and asset (`category`, `asset`: catalog/procedural/library.json, docs/PROCEDURAL.md); an item with `alias` is another item under its own name, category and first preset (the storm sea is the ocean on its storm preset). The library's other assets (built generators and placeholders) join the list from its registry when the viewer carries it.",
